A||N||2||Conrad Sanville||Alternator removal||||1||
Z||000000||Conrad Sanville||09-13-2000||10:09 PM||||<BR>I have to remove the alternator in my 85 <BR>2.5L. What is the easiest way? I've <BR>taken the alternator out of my GT <BR>through the bottom, the 2.5L looks like <BR>it is going to be tricky.  Any ideas?  <BR>Thanks.<P>------------------<BR><BR>Radcon||||reg||1
Z||000001||zeusrekning||09-13-2000||10:50 PM||||i unbolted mine and had to slide it over to the drivers side of the car so it could fit out the bottom only took a minute.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodrv6||09-13-2000||10:50 PM||||Remove the dogbone and the bracket that it attatches to on the engine.  The same bracket holds the top of the alternator. Disconnect the battery and the wires on the back of the alternator.  Remove the lower alternator pivot bolt and lift the alternator out the top.  If you try to go through the bottom, you'll have to remove the oil filter and the lower alternator bracket.  If you go out the top you don't have to crawl under the car at all.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE||||reg||1
